description:
Build and edit the environment block a child process receives (lesson 1.02). Here it is a `std::string` of `NAME=value` entries, each followed by a zero byte, with one more zero at the end (the real block is UTF-16, with exactly the same layout).

```cpp
using Variables = std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>>;

std::string buildBlock(const Variables& vars);
Variables parseBlock(const std::string& block);
std::string withVariable(const std::string& block, const std::string& name, const std::string& value);
std::string withoutVariable(const std::string& block, const std::string& name);
```

- **buildBlock** sorts the variables by name **ignoring case** (compare the names with every letter in upper case), and if two names are the same ignoring case, keeps only the **last** one given. An empty list gives a block of two zeros.
- **parseBlock** reads the entries back in order, splitting each at its first `=` **after the first character** (Windows keeps hidden entries like `=C:=C:\Work`, whose names start with `=`).
- **withVariable** returns a new block with the variable set (replacing any existing one with the same name ignoring case, and keeping the spelling of the new name); **withoutVariable** removes it.

